# Live Electron app (CDP MCP)

`npm run dev` runs the app with `--remote-debugging-port=9222`, connected to the
`project-0-blueberry-browser-chrome-devtools` MCP. Use it to reproduce bugs and
verify fixes live instead of guessing.

- Topbar, sidebar, and each tab are **separate CDP targets**. Use `list_pages`,
  then `select_page` before `navigate_page` / `evaluate_script` / `take_screenshot`.
- CDP **cannot** create/close/switch tabs (`Target.createTarget` "Not supported").
- Drive the main process via preload bridges with `evaluate_script` on the right page:
  - topbar → `window.topBarAPI` (`createTab(url)`, `closeTab`, `switchTab`, `tabRunJs`, `toggleSidebar`)
  - sidebar → `window.sidebarAPI` (`sendChatMessage`, `getMessages`, `clearChat`)
- Reusable snippets for CDP-unreachable actions live in `scripts/`.
